NEARS-482 QA — banner subtitle mojibake is BAKED INTO the backend banner PNG (not app-rendered)

Banner id=22 (zone 2, Organic Shop), image: storage/banner/d-ecc510bd18.png (900x350)
On-device the home promo banner shows garbled monospace text:
    "Save big this week â  Organic Shop"
The 'â' is the Latin-1 misdecode of em-dash U+2014 (UTF-8 E2 80 94 -> Latin-1 'â\x80\x94').

ROOT CAUSE: the text is rendered into the PNG pixels by the BACKEND placeholder-image
generator; it is NOT live Flutter Text. Proof:
- API banner title over the wire is clean & \u-escaped: "Save big this week — Organic Shop"
  (curl /api/v1/banners zoneId:[2] -> title decodes clean under BOTH Latin-1 and UTF-8).
- The reskinned banner widget (UserApp/lib/features/home/widgets/views/banner_view.dart,
  _PhotoHeroCard) renders ONLY: NearsBadge('limited_offer') + headline Text(store.name) +
  Claim Deal CTA — NO app-rendered subtitle. The headline "Organic Shop" is clean on-device.
- The mojibaked string is visible in the raw source PNG itself (bug-banner-image-baked-mojibake.png).

IMPACT: customer sees garbled text on the home promo banner.
SCOPE: OUTSIDE NEARS-482 (which fixes the app-side JSON UTF-8 decode; it cannot alter image pixels).
This is a backend/seed asset defect: regenerate the banner placeholder image with correct UTF-8.
